  title: [1985 Ford Ranger 4×4 5-Speed at No Reserve],
  author: [bringatrailer],
  source-name: [Bring a Trailer],
  images: (),
  paragraphs: (
  [This 1985 Ford Ranger 4×4 was purchased by the seller from the original owner in February 2026 after it had been parked in a garage for approximately a decade. Finished in Silver Metallic over Regatta Blue cloth and vinyl, the truck is powered by a 2.8-liter V6 linked with a five-speed manual transmission and a dual-range transfer case. Equipment includes a LEER bed topper, 14″ steel wheels, power steering, front disc brakes, and an Xtreme Sound cassette stereo. This Ranger is offered at no reserve with a clean Carfax report and a clean Ohio title in the seller’s name.],
  [The truck is finished in Silver Metallic (1E) with black bumpers and features a LEER bed topper, a bug shield, swing-away side mirrors, and mud flaps. Spots of rust on the left side were reportedly repaired under previous ownership, approximately 25 years ago.],
  [The 14″ steel wheels are mounted with 235/75 Republic Trail Mark Radial APR tires up front and Cooper Discoverer S/T rubber out back. The truck is equipped with power steering and manually locking front hubs, and braking is provided by front discs and rear drums. The seller tells us that the brake booster and shock absorbers were replaced in preparation for the sale.],
  [The bench seat is upholstered in Regatta Blue cloth and vinyl and is accompanied by a color-coordinated dashboard and door panels. Interior appointments include a vinyl floor liner, a cabin heater, an Xtreme Sound cassette stereo, and manual-crank windows. The dashboard pad is cracked, and rust is noted on the left floorboard by the drain plug.],
  [Instrumentation consists of an 85-mph speedometer and gauges for fuel level, oil pressure, coolant temperature, and amperage. The five-digit odometer shows 48k miles.],
  [The 2.8-liter V6 was serviced with an oil change and a replacement carburetor in preparation for the sale. There is a ticking noise from the engine, which the seller believes to be a sticking lifter.],
  [Power is sent to the rear or all four wheels through a five-speed manual transmission and a dual-range transfer case. The seller says that the fuel tank and straps were replaced in preparation for the sale. There is some rust on the undercarriage, and a coating has been applied.],
  [The Carfax report is free from accidents or other damage.],
),
